    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but a \"tiny break\" doesn't change the fact that i'm drowning. it feels like no matter how much i rest, the mountain of stuff i have to deal with is just waiting to crush me again the second i wake up. it's not just a bad week or a bad month. it's my whole existence. it feels like the only way to actually stop the crushing is to just stop existing entirely. is that even a rational thought to have?",
